    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50832" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱπποσύνη</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the art of driving the war-chariot</i>: generally,
				<i>driving, horsemanship</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱπποσύνῃ . . πεποιθώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.303
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				11.503
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξοχοι ἱπποσύνᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					108
				</span></i>
			 ( =
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.946
			</span></i>): in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λελασμένος ἱπποσυνάων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.776
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.40
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱπποσύνας ἐδίδαξαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.307
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i>horse, cavalry</i>, Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.141
			</span></i>.</div>
